# ── WHAT THIS STANDS BETWEEN, AND WHY IT GREW ─────────────────────────────
#
# A push to `main` is a deploy. `image` builds only once typecheck, lint,
# format, unit, checks, sql and build have all passed — seven gates — and this
# hook mirrored exactly ONE of them.
#
# On 2026-09-21 a deploy was blocked by two bullet characters. `docs/quality/
# debt-map.md` had `*` where Prettier writes `-`, CI failed on `format`, and
# `image` and `deploy` were skipped: the whole batch sat unshipped over a
# character that `bun run format` fixes without being asked. Nothing local had
# a reason to notice, because the hook only typechecks.
#
# So `format:check` joins it. It is the cheapest of the six missing gates and
# the only one that failed that day. `--cache` (in the script, so CI and this
# hook stay the SAME command) takes it from ~60s to ~10s after the first run;
# CI's runner has no cache and so still checks every file.
#
# NOT added, deliberately: `lint`, `build`, `sql` and the e2e suites, which are
# minutes each and would make pushing something people avoid. `test:unit` is
# under a second and is the obvious next candidate — propose it separately
# rather than folding it in here.
#
# A hook is a convenience, never the authority. CI is the authority, and
# nothing here may be weakened to make a push go through.
bun run typecheck
bun run format:check
